A1.2 Design the Storage
Use a stations table for metadata and readings for time-series measurements. A foreign key links them; a unique constraint prevents
duplicate station/time readings.
CREATE TABLE stations (
 station_id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
 station_name TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,
 source_temperature_unit TEXT NOT NULL
);
CREATE TABLE readings (
 reading_id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
 station_id INTEGER NOT NULL,
 reading_date TEXT NOT NULL,
 reading_hour INTEGER NOT NULL,
 pm25 REAL, pm10 REAL, no2 REAL, temperature_c REAL,
 FOREIGN KEY(station_id) REFERENCES stations(station_id),
 UNIQUE(station_id, reading_date, reading_hour)
);
CREATE INDEX idx_readings_station_date
ON readings(station_id, reading_date);
Mapping: station text is mapped to station_id; date is YYYY-MM-DD; hour is an integer; pollutant values are REAL; temperature is
converted to °C. Missing measurements become NULL. Rejected records and reasons are retained in an error log.
