A3.2 Daily Summary Table
Fields: station_id, reading_date, pm25_min, pm25_max, pm25_mean and valid_reading_count. Produce with:
SELECT station_id, reading_date,
 MIN(pm25) AS pm25_min, MAX(pm25) AS pm25_max,
 AVG(pm25) AS pm25_mean, COUNT(pm25) AS valid_reading_count
FROM readings
GROUP BY station_id, reading_date;
COUNT(pm25) ignores NULL values. A Python alternative keeps a dictionary keyed by (station, date) and updates min, max, sum
and count. Both scan n readings in O(n). A running dictionary uses O(g) memory for g station-day groups; storing all rows first uses
O(n).
